<speak>Separate purposes would suit me. If a meeting covers too many unrelated items, I spend the whole time wondering whether I have forgotten one of them. I can bring a short list, but I do not want it to become a stack of homework. For a relationship meeting, I would like a simple agenda in advance. For help with the digital inbox, just tell me to have the tablet available. For administrative changes, tell me which ordinary process to use. Then I know what kind of attention each appointment needs. I am much more relaxed when I know why something is in my diary.</speak>